{"id":"int-ce431035","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-21T04:52:29.755691Z","actor":"Stephen Jennings","issue_id":"bad-juju-6wo","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"VS Code status.jj documents are now served via a custom 'badjuju-status' URI scheme registered with a TextDocumentContentProvider, which makes them inherently readonly. The provider re-reads the file from disk and fires onDidChange on refresh so updates appear without conflicting with in-editor edits."}}
{"id":"int-93bbbda6","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-21T05:26:13.648833Z","actor":"Stephen Jennings","issue_id":"bad-juju-pi5","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Scoped 'r' and 'g' refresh keybindings to status.jj only (status is readonly so single-letter shortcuts are safe). Log buffer is now free for typing revset characters. Added OUTPUT: heading and a COMMAND REFERENCE section to log.jj. Updated status.jj COMMAND REFERENCE to match real keybindings (n=new, l=open log, d=describe, g=refresh, q=close — removed stale 'c=commit' and 'r=rebase' entries)."}}
{"id":"int-6a1a2eb2","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-21T05:45:48.419263Z","actor":"Stephen Jennings","issue_id":"bad-juju-7fr","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Implemented: server renders Mutable/Stack revset shortcuts as JJ: comment lines under REVSET in log.jj; VS Code extension tracks cursor position via badjuju.onLogShortcutLine context key and rebinds Enter on shortcut lines to apply the revset and refresh. All 37 cargo tests pass with no warnings; biome and clippy clean. UI keybinding behavior not exercised in a running VS Code instance — server-side rendering and command logic are tested."}}
{"id":"int-a5e1a081","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-21T05:55:08.744125Z","actor":"Stephen Jennings","issue_id":"bad-juju-u8h","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Capture cursor line/char before triggering log refresh; wait for VS Code's file-watcher reload (via onDidChangeTextDocument, 1s timeout) before restoring cursor — avoids race where VS Code's auto-reload would reposition the cursor after our setSelection. Restores cursor to same (clamped) line/char so the user stays on the shortcut line they just activated. Biome/clippy/tests clean."}}
